<h1>Purge Sort</h1>
<p>
    Purge Sort goes through the array,
    checking if each element is smaller than the previous.
    If it is, Purge Sort will remove it from the array, 
    then continue to the next element.
    <br>
    <br>
    The average and worst-case Time Complexity of 
    Purge Sort depends on which method is being used to delete elements,
    with <b>Shifting</b> giving it a Time Complexity of <b>n<sup>2</sup></b>,
    and <b>Swapping</b> and <b>Gaps</b> giving it a Time Complexity of <b>n</b>.
</p>

